---
layout: base.njk
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/lineage.css">
<article class="lineage-page" id="trails-page">
  <nav class="lineage-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/map/knowledge-lineage/">Knowledge map</a> / Follow a thread</nav>
  <p class="kicker">Working prototype · Unreviewed · 10 November 2026</p>
  <h1>Follow a thread.</h1>
  <p class="lineage-deck">See how a claim changed, or what follows a reported discovery.</p>

  <nav class="lineage-choices" aria-label="Choose a trail">
    {% for trail in lineage.trails %}<a href="#{{ trail.id }}"><span>{{ trail.eyebrow | escape }}</span><strong>{{ trail.title | escape }}</strong></a>{% endfor %}
  </nav>
<p class="lineage-reading-key">Read the story first. Open a card’s evidence when you want to check it.</p>
  {% for trail in lineage.trails %}
  <section id="{{ trail.id }}" class="lineage-trail" aria-labelledby="{{ trail.id }}-title">
    <p class="kicker">{{ trail.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
    <h2 id="{{ trail.id }}-title">{{ trail.title | escape }}</h2>
    <p>{{ trail.intro | escape }}</p>
    {% if trail.id == 'finding' %}<figure class="lineage-overview">
      <a href="/notes/knowledge-lineage/finding.svg"><img src="/notes/knowledge-lineage/finding.svg" alt="Four records with labelled arrows: earlier essay cites the source account; later review challenges the earlier wording; corrected claim revises that wording. These are directed evidence links, not causes. Open the drawing for direct record links." width="360" height="478"></a>
      <figcaption>The arrows point to the account each record cites, challenges or revises. Open the drawing to follow its record links, or read the trail below.</figcaption>
    </figure>{% endif %}
    <figure class="lineage-figure" aria-labelledby="{{ trail.id }}-caption">
      <ol class="lineage-steps">
        {% for step in trail.steps %}
        <li id="{{ step.id }}" class="lineage-step">
          <div class="lineage-card">
            <p class="lineage-kind">{{ step.kind | escape }}</p>
            <h3><a href="{{ step.record_url }}">{{ step.title | escape }}</a></h3>
            <p>{{ step.summary | escape }}</p>
            <details class="lineage-source-details"><summary>Evidence and dates</summary>
            <dl class="lineage-clocks">
              <div><dt>{{ step.date_label | escape }}</dt><dd>{{ step.event_date or 'Not established' }}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Retained source read</dt><dd>{{ step.source_read_date or 'Not a source-read event' }}</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p class="lineage-ai">{{ step.ai_role | escape }}</p>
            <p class="lineage-records"><a href="{{ step.evidence.url }}">Exact retained passage</a>{% if step.primary_url %} · <a href="{{ step.primary_url }}">Original source</a>{% endif %}</p>
            </details>
          </div>
          {% for connection in step.connections %}
          <details class="lineage-connection connection-{{ connection.status }}">
            <summary><span class="lineage-status">{{ connection.status | capitalize }}</span> This {{ connection.predicate | replace('attributes-to', 'attributes its reading to') | replace('reports-on', 'reports on') | replace('asks-about', 'asks about') | escape }}: {{ connection.objectTitle | escape }} <span class="lineage-open">· inspect</span></summary>
            <p>{{ connection.qualification | escape }}</p>
            <p><a href="#{{ connection.object }}">Jump to the related account</a> · <a href="/map/knowledge-lineage/evidence/#relation-{{ connection.id }}">Read this connection and its evidence</a></p>
          </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
      <figcaption id="{{ trail.id }}-caption">{{ trail.limit | escape }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% if trail.id == 'finding' %}
      <aside class="lineage-aside"><h3>A gap can be part of the story</h3>
      <p>A reviewer could not read seven Australia claims. A later verification checked the source account and preserved that earlier failure. An inaccessible source is a gap in our view.</p>
      <p><a href="/notes/it-was-only-a-test/claims-check-claude/">The original failed reads</a> · <a href="/notes/it-was-only-a-test/australia-verification/">The later verification</a> · <a href="/notes/R-0053-it-was-only-a-test-correction/">The correction record</a></p>
      <p><a href="/essays/it-was-only-a-test/">Read It was only a test</a></p></aside>
    {% else %}
      <aside class="lineage-aside"><h3>Where the trail stops</h3>
      <p>The private report date is unknown in the retained disclosure brief. The watch cannot tell whether machines installed a fix. Neither a severity score nor a prediction measures successful exploitation or social benefit.</p>
      <p><a href="/investigations/model-found-bugs/">Continue with When a model finds the bug</a> · <a href="/studies/LH038/brief/">What the disclosure protocol will test</a></p></aside>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="lineage-next">{% if trail.id == 'finding' %}<a href="#topic">Next trail: what happens after a reported discovery?</a>{% else %}<a href="#finding">Back to the claim: what changed after review?</a>{% endif %}</p>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
  <details class="lineage-bridge"><summary>Why these threads sit together</summary><section aria-labelledby="bridge-title">
    <p class="kicker">Suggested connection · Inferred</p>
    <h2 id="bridge-title">The same question, in different settings</h2>
    <p>What does a source report, and what can we establish from it? Both trails make that distinction useful. This is a navigation suggestion by the pilot author, not evidence that either investigation influenced the other.</p>
    <p><a href="{{ lineage.candidates[0].evidence.url }}">The shared evidence principle</a></p>
  </section></details>
  <p><a href="/map/knowledge-lineage/evidence/">Explore the evidence record</a> · <a href="/map/knowledge-lineage/">Back to the knowledge map</a></p>
</article>
